WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.800
What's the product of 33 and 21?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.900
Pause the video and try to solve it.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:25.000
The traditional way, is to write '21 under 33'.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.280
Then '3 times 1 is 3', '3 times 1 is 3' again!

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:36.440
Write a zero here, '3 times 2 is 6' and '3 times 2 is 6'.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.580
396. '33 times 21' is 693.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.840
But this took a lot of time.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.940
Want to see a better way?

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.320
Okay, here goes!

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.520
3 times 2 is '06',

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:58.740
3 times 1 is '03' and we add this product with this one.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.480
6 plus 3 is 09, 693.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.220
Took us less than 5 seconds.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.280
Don't worry! By the end of this video

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.240
you will be very comfortable multiplying two-digit numbers.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.540
First digits of both then second digits of both

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:19.780
and then the umbrella approach.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.860
Product of these two, plus the product of these two.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.380
With the same approach, what will be '43 times 17'?

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.560
Pause and try.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:41.140
'4 times 1 is 04', '3 times 7 is 21'.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.600
'3 times 1 plus 4 times 7 is 31'.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:51.680
1, '2 plus 1' is 3 and '4 plus 3' is 7.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.200
731 is the answer.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.840
Easy, wasn't it?

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.740
But wait, where exactly do we write these numbers?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.320
The unit's digit of these numbers,

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.440
should be under the second digit from the right of the number on top.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:12.120
Hence, we wrote the 9 under the 0 and the 1 under the 2.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.440
If you forget which products to add

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.280
just think of an umbrella or a mushroom.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.340
Product of these 2, plus the product of these 2.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.760
Now take a slightly tougher one.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.440
'76 times 97'. Give it a try.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.780
It's easy.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.320
Just that the numbers are bigger this time.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:46.140
'7 times 9 is 63' and '6 times 7 is 42'.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:52.140
'9 times 6 plus 7 times 7' is '54 plus 49',

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.980
which is '103'.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.000
We wrote the three under the second digit from right of the number on top.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.140
Two, four plus three is seven.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:05.500
Three, six plus one is seven.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:09.940
7372 is our answer.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.440
63 is the product of the first digits of each number,

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.800
42 is the product of the second digits of each number.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.920
And 103 is the sum of the product of these two

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.660
and the product of these two numbers.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.100
Here are three examples for you

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.540
which you should be able to solve it 30 seconds flat.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.960
15 seconds ideally,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.740
but I'm giving you 30 assuming it's your first time.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.480
'31 times 24',

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.180
'62 times 27',

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.740
'38 times 92'. Your time starts now!

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.340
Let's solve this quickly.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:28.760
'3 times 2 is 06',  '1 times 4 is 04' and '2 plus 12 is 14'.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.300
744 is the correct answer.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.250
Okay, next.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.680
'6 times 2 is 12',

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.240
'2 times 7 is 14' and '4 plus 42 is 46'.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.020
1674 is the answer.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:56.480
The last one. '3 times 9 is 27', '8 times 2 is 16' and '72 plus 6 is 78'.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.140
6, 1 plus 8 is 9.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.780
7 plus 7 is 14.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.280
We write a 4 and carry the 1 over.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.680
1 plus 2 is 3.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.400
38 times 92 is 3496.

